    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0308" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg248"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Worthington.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 19, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit herewith, for your information,
                    a copy of an instruction<anchor n="†" xml:id="d171-f1"/> addressed by this
                    department to James Watson Webb, esq., United States minister to Rio de Janeiro,
                    relative to the recent refusal of the Brazilian commander on the Parana River to
                    allow the United States ship of war Wasp to pass the blockade of that river for
                    the purpose of conveying Mr. Washburn on his return to the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry G. Worthington,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d171-f1" n="†" xml:id="d171-f1-content">
                <p>For this inclosure see instruction No. 233, August 17, 1868, to the United States
                    minister to prazil.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
